040507             0744*   ; Calculate the expected RGBA2222 payload size.
040507             0745*   ; inputs:  width and height in agnb_metadata
040507             0746*   ; outputs: HL = width * height (unsigned 24-bit)
040507             0747*   ;          u32 result retained in agnb_expected_data_size
040507             0748*   ; destroys: AF, HL
040507             0749*   ;
040507             0750*   ; IMPORTANT: umul24 discards product bits above bit 23. That theoretical limit
040507             0751*   ; is 16,777,215 bytes/pixels--orders of magnitude larger than any conceivable
040507             0752*   ; bitmap on the Agon. The initial image loader therefore deliberately uses the
040507             0753*   ; smaller native-ADL result instead of carrying a general u16*u16=u32 routine.
040507             0754*   agnb_calculate_image_data_size:
040507             0755*   ; Load each contiguous u16 field as UHL, then use the established eZ80 idiom
040507             0756*   ; to discard the accidentally loaded following byte.
